 "segments": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 3.4,
   "t": "Nine hospitals suspected him. Every single one chose silence."
  },
  {
   "s": 4.32,
   "e": 8.14,
   "t": "Somerset Medical Center was by no means his initial crime scene."
  },
  {
   "s": 9.26,
   "e": 16.78,
   "t": "Across 16 years, from 1988 to 2003, Charles Cullen had worked across nine different hospitals"
  },
  {
   "s": 16.78,
   "e": 19.76,
   "t": "and one nursing home spanning New Jersey and Pennsylvania."
  },
  {
   "s": 20.88,
   "e": 25.9,
   "t": "Wherever he took up employment, nighttime cardiac arrest fatalities consistently spiked"
  },
  {
   "s": 25.9,
   "e": 27.84,
   "t": "along an anomalous statistical curve."
  },
  {
   "s": 28.9,
   "e": 34.0,
   "t": "Whenever suspicion mounted, he was quietly forced out with neutral references, allowing"
  },
  {
   "s": 34.0,
   "e": 38.78,
   "t": "him to seamlessly transfer to another facility and resume his predatory trajectory."
  },
  {
   "s": 40.0,
   "e": 45.38,
   "t": "However, based on epidemiological reviews and massive unexplained medication deficits,"
  },
  {
   "s": 46.02,
   "e": 50.04,
   "t": "investigative analysts believe the true toll could reach 400 lives."
  },
  {
   "s": 50.04,
   "e": 56.64,
   "t": "But systemic silence transformed institutions dedicated to healing into inadvertent sanctuaries"
  },
  {
   "s": 56.64,
   "e": 58.98,
   "t": "for serial homicide across 16 years."
  },
  {
   "s": 59.82,
   "e": 66.08,
   "t": "In 2004, the governor of New Jersey enacted the Landmark Cullen Act to permanently dismantle"
  },
  {
   "s": 66.08,
   "e": 67.84,
   "t": "dangerous institutional silence."
  },
  {
   "s": 69.04,
   "e": 70.46,
   "t": "Episode 4 of Amber Eyes."
  },
  {
   "s": 70.76,
   "e": 72.76,
   "t": "Watch the full documentary via the bio-link."
  }
 ]
}